<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Napoleonic Wars</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1803–1815</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Napoleonic Wars were a series of wars between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and shifting coalitions of European powers from 1803 to 1815. They ended with Napoleon's defeat at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-waterloo">Waterloo</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/congress-of-vienna">Congress of Vienna</a>. Because the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-netherlands">Netherlands</a> fell under French control, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a> colonies and trading posts across the world, returning some in 1814 to 1816 and keeping others.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/napoleonic-wars.jpg" alt="Napoleonic Wars" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ruedi33a · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Napoleonic_Wars_(revision).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
